# 5. MUSIC CATALOG INTEGRATION

Use MusicBrainz as the primary source for music metadata.

Use Cover Art Archive for artwork retrieval.

Important requirements:

- Search the local database before calling external APIs.
- Use external identifiers to avoid duplicate records.
- Store provider identifiers.
- Handle missing artwork gracefully.
- Handle missing metadata gracefully.
- Implement API request throttling.
- Cache metadata.
- Avoid excessive external API requests.
- Respect provider attribution and licensing requirements.

Understand the difference between:
- Artist.
- Release group.
- Release.
- Track.
- Recording.

Use release groups as the primary album-level representation initially.

Support multiple artists per album.

Do not assume every album has a single artist.

Build a reusable music provider integration layer so additional providers can be introduced later.

Never fabricate catalog data or artwork.

